Under `--type-system-refresh --contextual-lambda-domains`, resolution no longer crashes with an `InvalidCastException` when the omitted parameter type of a function-result lambda is taken from the declared arrow domain and the parameter is passed to a formal whose type names the same type through a type synonym (possibly generic, or naming a subset type or a newtype), as in `function f(): seq<int> -> bool { x => g(x) }` with `function g(x: A): bool` and `type A = seq<int>`. Subset constraints of the formal are still checked (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/390).
